## 9. Workflow Protocol

### Schema First
1. Define SQL in Supabase
2. Update Swift models to match
3. Write service layer
4. Build UI

### Git Commit Style
- `feat:` New feature
- `fix:` Bug fix
- `safety:` Safety-related changes (CRITICAL)
- `ui:` UI changes

### The Test Loop
1. Write code
2. Run Maestro test
3. If fail → AI reads screenshot → Auto-fix
4. Repeat until pass

---

## 10. What NOT To Do

### NEVER:
- Auto-save medical data without confirmation
- Use pure black (#000000) - causes OLED smearing
- Put buttons in top 70% of screen for primary actions
- Give medical advice in AI responses
- Turn off RLS in Supabase
- Store API keys in code
- Use cartoonish/cutesy UI elements
- Send notifications for minor log edits

### ALWAYS:
- Show Ghost Log draft before saving
- Use haptic feedback on save/warning
- Scope all queries to family_id
- Test safety logic exhaustively
- Dark mode by default
- 48pt minimum touch targets
